1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,490
Your universe works, and a crew can sit down and play it for an evening.

2
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:07,398
This class is about the evening after that,

3
00:00:07,848 --> 00:00:09,372
and the eighteen after that.

4
00:00:11,172 --> 00:00:15,478
Today you'll give your crew a question that takes twenty evenings to answer.

5
00:00:16,378 --> 00:00:18,606
And you'll find out, by measuring it,

6
00:00:19,056 --> 00:00:22,376
exactly what the game remembers from one week to the next.

7
00:00:23,576 --> 00:00:27,723
The people who make the game built a campaign on the same machinery you're using.

8
00:00:28,623 --> 00:00:30,088
It's called Storm's Beacon,

9
00:00:30,538 --> 00:00:33,462
and they wrote down what they decided as they went.

10
00:00:35,262 --> 00:00:38,100
First, every episode goes round one loop.

11
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:42,336
Someone names a place, the crew goes, finds one thing out,

12
00:00:42,786 --> 00:00:44,952
gets interrupted, and reports back.

13
00:00:45,852 --> 00:00:49,380
Second, only three evenings are written by hand.

14
00:00:49,830 --> 00:00:51,473
The rest come from one pattern.

15
00:00:52,373 --> 00:00:55,295
Third, they built the pattern before they wrote the episodes.

16
00:00:57,095 --> 00:00:59,038
And they were honest about the hard part.

17
00:00:59,938 --> 00:01:01,388
It isn't the machinery.

18
00:01:01,838 --> 00:01:03,716
It's having enough for the crew to do.

19
00:01:04,916 --> 00:01:09,877
So let's look at what you have, the way a crew sees it on the first night.

20
00:01:10,777 --> 00:01:13,581
There are four leads, and all four are open.

21
00:01:15,381 --> 00:01:17,310
For one evening, that's generous.

22
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:20,599
For a campaign, it's the whole map in the first minute.

23
00:01:21,499 --> 00:01:24,709
Three things change when the same people come back.

24
00:01:26,509 --> 00:01:28,374
You show them one lead at a time.

25
00:01:29,274 --> 00:01:32,175
A win belongs to the very last evening.

26
00:01:33,075 --> 00:01:35,898
And only what the game keeps is still true next week.

27
00:01:37,098 --> 00:01:39,651
The plan for a campaign isn't for the game,

28
00:01:40,101 --> 00:01:43,109
and it isn't for the crew. It's for you.

29
00:01:44,009 --> 00:01:47,359
So it goes in a plain page beside the universe file.

30
00:01:49,159 --> 00:01:50,942
A premise: one question.

31
00:01:51,392 --> 00:01:54,997
Five boats and forty-one people are missing.

32
00:01:55,897 --> 00:01:57,956
A pressure that's true every single week.

33
00:01:58,406 --> 00:02:00,439
Somebody else is stripping those boats.

34
00:02:01,339 --> 00:02:03,600
And the loop, in five lines.

35
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:07,267
Lint doesn't read this page,

36
00:02:07,717 --> 00:02:09,059
and neither does the game.

37
00:02:09,959 --> 00:02:13,775
I tried, with a page made to look exactly like a record.

38
00:02:14,975 --> 00:02:16,931
Now the part the game does read.

39
00:02:17,831 --> 00:02:20,402
One landmark, a lifeboat called the Wren.

40
00:02:20,852 --> 00:02:22,839
And one lead that sends the crew to her.

41
00:02:24,639 --> 00:02:27,590
You know every line of these from the last class.

42
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:29,593
Three habits are new.

43
00:02:30,493 --> 00:02:32,395
The lead's text is a page,

44
00:02:32,845 --> 00:02:36,748
so I give it three short paragraphs, with an empty line between them.

45
00:02:37,648 --> 00:02:40,419
What happened, where to go, and why tonight.

46
00:02:42,219 --> 00:02:44,454
The landmark stays one line,

47
00:02:44,904 --> 00:02:48,110
because the arrival card shows only its first line.

48
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:52,034
The title starts with the campaign's name,

49
00:02:52,484 --> 00:02:55,707
because in week six the Quest Log is a long list.

50
00:02:56,607 --> 00:02:59,158
And the key starts with the evening's number,

51
00:02:59,608 --> 00:03:01,905
because you're going to write sixty of them.

52
00:03:03,105 --> 00:03:05,151
I save, and I run lint,

53
00:03:05,601 --> 00:03:07,674
and it says clean.

54
00:03:09,474 --> 00:03:12,831
Now look at the count: one universe file, one story file.

55
00:03:13,731 --> 00:03:15,581
The campaign page isn't counted,

56
00:03:16,031 --> 00:03:18,526
which is exactly what we want.

57
00:03:19,726 --> 00:03:22,950
This next part is the measurement the whole class stands on.

58
00:03:23,850 --> 00:03:25,222
I pay the levy,

59
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:26,894
I take a job,

60
00:03:27,344 --> 00:03:30,043
I follow the lead out to the Wren, and I come home.

61
00:03:31,843 --> 00:03:34,093
Then I write down six things.

62
00:03:34,544 --> 00:03:37,501
Where the ship is. The credits. The standing.

63
00:03:38,401 --> 00:03:39,844
The lead, the job,

64
00:03:40,294 --> 00:03:41,791
and the charted places.

65
00:03:43,591 --> 00:03:45,599
Now I close the game. All of it.

66
00:03:46,499 --> 00:03:48,157
And I type the same line again.

67
00:03:49,957 --> 00:03:51,365
It's the same system,

68
00:03:51,815 --> 00:03:54,300
the same credits, and the same standing.

69
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,810
The lead is still done,

70
00:03:57,260 --> 00:03:58,648
the job is still mine,

71
00:03:59,098 --> 00:04:01,186
and the Wren is still on the chart.

72
00:04:02,386 --> 00:04:04,052
So that's a campaign's memory.

73
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:05,803
Where the ship is,

74
00:04:06,253 --> 00:04:08,254
what the side has in the bank,

75
00:04:08,704 --> 00:04:10,610
and what every side thinks of this ship.

76
00:04:12,410 --> 00:04:13,605
Every step of the story,

77
00:04:14,055 --> 00:04:16,437
done, open, or still hidden.

78
00:04:17,337 --> 00:04:18,450
The jobs in hand,

79
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:20,612
and every place they've charted.

80
00:04:22,412 --> 00:04:24,721
That's enough to build twenty evenings on.

81
00:04:25,921 --> 00:04:27,577
And here's what it doesn't keep.

82
00:04:28,027 --> 00:04:29,026
It's a short list.

83
00:04:30,826 --> 00:04:33,215
Guards the crew ran away from are back.

84
00:04:34,115 --> 00:04:37,194
And a universe with a new title is a new game,

85
00:04:37,644 --> 00:04:39,285
so choose the title once.

86
00:04:41,085 --> 00:04:43,774
Some things you might expect to lose are kept.

87
00:04:44,674 --> 00:04:47,838
A clock that was running comes back with the time it had left.

88
00:04:48,738 --> 00:04:51,967
A ship you rename keeps its standing and its jobs.

89
00:04:53,767 --> 00:04:56,221
And the game can remember a fact of your story.

90
00:04:57,121 --> 00:04:58,531
That's the next lecture.

91
00:04:59,731 --> 00:05:01,928
So you have a premise, a first lead,

92
00:05:02,378 --> 00:05:04,311
and a table you measured yourself.

93
00:05:06,111 --> 00:05:08,381
End every evening the same way:

94
00:05:08,831 --> 00:05:10,939
jump home, then close the game.

95
00:05:11,839 --> 00:05:15,274
Next time, we build a whole evening round that one lead.
